    "category": "Automatic catchweighing instrument",
    "type_designations": [
      "L-Series 2180",
      "Express",
      "Force",
      "L2150"
    ],
    "description": "Battery-operated automatic catchweighing instrument (Category Y), designated the L-Series 2180, comprising an electronic indicator, pressure transducer and sensors mounted on a wheeled loader. The pattern automatically determines the load in the bucket during the lifting process: the hydraulic pressure in the loader's arms is converted by a pressure transducer, the output being used by the indicator to display the corresponding weight. Alternatives cover modified software (MMS reporting via data module and wireless communication, not for legal purposes), reduced-functionality models Express and Force, the L2150 with modified indicator console layout and dedicated target weight key, forks instead of a bucket, replacement of the AAA-20710 position sensor by any compatible sensor, and mounting on container reach stackers (weighing inhibited when the telescopic boom is not fully retracted) or container forklifts."
